#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:0
msgid ""
"Record a video of your whole screen or a selected region on Ubuntu Desktop, "
"and enable hardware acceleration for better performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:8
msgid "Record the screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:10
msgid ""
"You can record a video of your screen. The video either captures your whole "
"screen or a selected region. It's saved as a WebM or MP4 video file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:12
msgid "Press {kbd}`PrintScr` and switch to {guilabel}`Record Screen`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:14
msgid "Alternatively, press {kbd}`Ctrl+Alt+Shift+R`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:16
msgid "Select what to record:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:18
msgid "{guilabel}`Selection` records a screen region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:19
msgid "{guilabel}`Screen` records your whole screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:21
msgid "Click {guilabel}`Capture` or press {kbd}`Enter`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:23
msgid ""
"A red indicator in the top panel shows that you're recording and for how "
"long."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:25
msgid "To stop the recording, click the red indicator in the top panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:27
msgid ""
"Find the recording in the `Videos/Screencasts` folder in your home directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:30
msgid "Hardware acceleration for improved recording"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:32
msgid ""
"To improve performance and save battery life on laptops, you can enable "
"hardware acceleration for video encoding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:34
msgid ""
"By default, your screen recording relies on your CPU. This might cause "
"skipped frames or higher resource usage, even if you don't immediately "
"notice stuttering. Many computers have dedicated hardware for video encoding "
"using VA-API (Video Acceleration API), which is more efficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:36
msgid ""
"You can select third-party drivers in the Ubuntu installer to enable "
"hardware acceleration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:38
msgid ""
"On any Ubuntu release that's already installed and running, install packages "
"that provide hardware acceleration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/record-the-screen.md:49
msgid ""
"Certain GPU models and drivers don't support VA-API. With these, screen "
"recording will still rely on the CPU even after installing the extra "
"packages."
msgstr ""
